subissues.description:
Read WORKER-CONTRACT.md (workspace root) before starting. Human checkpoints (approve, record-ruling, accept-promotion, authorize-write grants) are run by the operator. Ligature is open-ended: file an epic #1 report only when Ligature fails at what it claims to do; record by-design limits as findings.

On scratch copies only, probe Ligature 1.4.2 end to end:
- a descriptor with several crates and per-cluster owners;
- whether anything consumes verifier_policy.supporting;
- check-bridges dispatch when a bridge crosses clusters with different owners;
- record-assurance for all three verifiers in one workspace;
- the workspace closure_kind with mixed clusters;
- G14/G17 behavior for CG1;
- crate configuration for Creusot and Kani (configure-crate has only cargo-verus).
Record each result. File epic #1 reports only for confirmed failures of what Ligature claims to do.
